turn is\nterminal for that delivery and preserves the first return error across retry.\nExercise literal Source/coordinator dispatch and holder-return bodies with\nexplicitly modeled installation, standing and Main-loop entry inputs, keeping\nall earlier controls. Ready retention alone supplies no CPU operation use,\naction Original, Source activation, ACK, ActionReturn or launched qualification.\n\nAt the actual Main control boundary retain its genuine CONTROL descriptor/group\nuse and QOM CPU reference with the Source allocation receipt and generation.\nAuthenticate the exact installed core dispatch field, thread/process and real\nCPU roster before publishing a distinct factual Native frame. Before independent\npost retain an exact paid Source borrower of the Ready handoff, canonical module\npayload field, first-bound child/member and standing lender. Neither copied\nholders nor first_cpu equality issues this loan or CPU operation permission.\n\nKeep the Main invocation/return journal separate from Stop admission. Preserve\nborn-negative outputs; block Ready, payload and delivery cleanup while a real\nMain borrower remains. Close actual QOM and Native descriptor dependencies before\nconsuming the Source holder and independently checking post. Retain uncertain\ntransitions, and never resurrect physical custody after a negative post. Actual\nnested masks prevent return; real QOM finalizers run while the descriptor/frame\nand Source borrower remain pinned. Keep fixed pools and all existing limits.\n\nExercise literal Core dispatch, Native registry and Source borrower bodies with\nreal mutex/thread/process identity, QOM reference/finalizer execution and actual\nnested mask return. Installed publication, allocator observation, Main/BQL entry\nand a minimal CPU class remain explicitly modeled component inputs. Preserve all\nearlier scenarios and causal controls. This physical custody cut grants no CPU\noperation, entered action Original, publisher membership, activation, ACK,\nActionReturn, peer return or launched lifecycle/VM qualification.\n\nFirst-bind v4 member callbacks for one prepaid nominal module-payload lifetime\nborrow under the exact Main owner. Authenticate the canonical payload field and\nlocal serial through the retained child journal. Keep older member editions\nexplicitly borrow-unavailable, and refuse half-pairs before member birth.\n\nJournal invocation before the masked callback, keeping exact stable holder and\nserial output fields. Accept known absence only from a genuine empty NULL/0\nnegative refusal; retain unknown or contradictory outputs. Preserve born-negative\nrecords and independent acquire/status/post facts. Release authenticates the\nactual born token and original serial, clears both original output fields, and\nrecords real consumption before independent callback status and Source post.\nNeither a scalar output nor a copied field can close the physical dependency.\n\nThe actual Core Main exit attempts module return before QOM, Native descriptor\nand Source borrower return. Unknown or unconsumed module debt retains those exact\nowners and the Ready handoff, blocks parent teardown and subsequent dispatch,\nand ends the real entered marker. No stale Main phase authorizes later retry;\na genuine cleanup entry producer remains required for that terminal containment.\n\nExercise literal Native/Source/Core consumers with a modeled module journal,\nexplicitly modeled installed publication/allocation/Main entry inputs, genuine\nmutex/process/thread identity, exact field custody and independent post errors.\nPreserve existing scenarios and limits. Local opaque lifetime borrowing exports\nno payload reference, action/class, entered Original, publisher membership, CPU\noperation permission, activation, ACK, ActionReturn or physical peer return.\nIt does not qualify the actual module/QEMU pairing or launched lifecycle.\n\nRequire CRUCSRV4/schema4 standing records with big-endian producer-retention\nedition1 at offset196. Preserve the 1496/1504/1520 publication extents and\nprocess-purpose8 envelope. Bind the declaration in the sealed initial record,\nrequire it on subsequent observations and reject every predecessor, zero and\nunknown edition before producing output. Rename every actual decoder caller,\nincluding the preinit literal closure, and refresh exact fixture fingerprints.\n\nDocument the producer promise: every born row, including dirty/unprojected\nrows, stays retained; exposed matching actions are irrevocably pending before\nrequest publication and cannot race unpublished abandonment. Exact action birth\ncannot be replaced until authenticated assigned-peer local closure. Local\nsubscriber closure never retires publisher-owned rows, and producer death or\nunknown cleanup does not certify physical return. This compatibility cut does\nnot yet construct a Source subscription or issue operation/action authority.\n\nExercise current syntax plus predecessor, edition, byte-order and unchanged\noutput refusals. Retain prior native causal timeout and launched lifecycle\nfailures as unresolved observations; no decoder or component result qualifies\nactivation, Original, publisher membership, ACK or ActionReturn.\n\nComplete the lifetime component's real constructor-RCU prerequisite before its\nforeign-process identity control forks. A child otherwise can restart RCU while\ninheriting the thread-registry mutex held by the vanished constructor helper.\nDrain actual RCU callbacks, then inspect the real registry under that mutex:\nexactly one retained RCU_RESTART helper, its coordinator, no overflow and no\nin-flight starts. Expose the actual starts counter in process-private inventory\nonly. Keep the helper record alive, every process-refusal assertion and all\nexisting build/test ceilings. No sleep, synthetic readiness or fork grant is\nsubstituted. Refresh exact extractor fingerprints after the native header edit.\n\nThe fixture starts no other QEMU threads in this scenario; actual callback\ncompletion follows thread registration, start-end consumption and RCU reader\nregistration. This closes a concrete inherited-lock race, not the production\nhot-fork admission contract. Independently rebuilt retained-start debt refuses\nbefore fork. Preserve failed prior causal attempts and the mandatory launched\nSource/Root lifecycle refusal until their respective fresh checks qualify.";
